1
00:00:00,040 --> 00:00:02,530
Tesla just made its Roadster FLY.

2
00:00:02,608 --> 00:00:04,540
It drove up a curved ramp until it hung

3
00:00:04,560 --> 00:00:05,780
upside down…

4
00:00:05,800 --> 00:00:07,940
then launched off, rolled itself upright

5
00:00:07,960 --> 00:00:09,980
in midair, and landed.

6
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:11,980
Tesla says fans pull air from under the

7
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:13,980
car, pinning it to the ramp.

8
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:16,500
In the air, jets of compressed gas help

9
00:00:16,520 --> 00:00:17,660
control the roll.

10
00:00:17,680 --> 00:00:19,660
It even cleared five of Tesla's own

11
00:00:19,680 --> 00:00:21,900
vehicles a Semi included.

12
00:00:21,920 --> 00:00:24,420
But the version that flies is the Rocket:

13
00:00:24,440 --> 00:00:26,260
invite-only, one seat.

14
00:00:26,280 --> 00:00:28,180
And Tesla's own page says it isn't

15
00:00:28,200 --> 00:00:29,860
approved for public roads.

16
00:00:29,880 --> 00:00:32,750
That 0 to 60 in 0.81 seconds?

17
00:00:33,040 --> 00:00:34,660
Tesla's own test.

18
00:00:34,680 --> 00:00:36,940
Production is targeted for 2028.

19
00:00:36,960 --> 00:00:38,837
So yes, the demo flew.

20
00:00:39,400 --> 00:00:40,740
The flying commute?

21
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:42,160
Still a question.

